    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d622">

                <pb facs="0698" n="688" xml:id="pg688"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Moscow/92: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the American Delegation
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-10-31T02:00:00-04:00">October 31, 1943—2
                            a.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1143. Amdel 63. For McDermott. Reference Department’s 1138<anchor n="52"
                        xml:id="d622-f1"/> and your 1788<anchor n="53" xml:id="d622-f2"/> (Amdel 61
                    and Delam 43). In order to synchronize the plans outlined in our messages under
                    reference we propose to give correspondents in Washington text of documents at 2
                    p.m. for publication at 5 p.m., Eastern War Time, November 1st. As indicated in
                    our 1138, no assurance possible here that German stories will not be rebroadcast
                    or published in this country in advance of agreed release time.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
